<title>NETHERLANDS: Dutch September cash retail sales fall 2.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Dutch September cash retail sales fall 2.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>VOORBURG, Netherlands 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch retail sales fell 2.2 percent in cash terms in September compared with September 1995, the Central Bureau of Statistics (CBS) said.</p>
<p>In volume terms September retail sales were 2.1 percent lower than in September 1996, the CBS added.  </p>
<p>DUTCH RETAIL SALES		    Sept 96   Aug 96   Jan-Sept 96</p>
<p> Pct change cash yr/yr		  -2.2	7.5	  3.2</p>
<p>     index (base 1994)		   104	106</p>
<p> Pct change prices yr/yr		-0.1     -0.6	 -0.2</p>
<p> Pct change volume yr/yr		-2.1	8.1	  3.3</p>
<p>     index (base 1994)		   104	108</p>
<p>DUTCH RETAIL SALES IN DETAIL	Sept 96   Aug 96   Jan-Sept 96</p>
<p>							(pct change yr/yr)</p>
<p> Food cash				  -4.6     +6.9	 +2.3</p>
<p> Food prices				-0.3     -0.9	 -0.2</p>
<p> Food volume				-4.2     +7.9	 +2.5</p>
<p> Durable goods &amp; non-food cash	-1.4     +8.5	 +3.7</p>
<p> Durable goods &amp; non-food prices    -0.1     -0.4	 -0.2</p>
<p> Durable goods &amp; non-food volume    -1.3     +8.9	 +3.9</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
